1
00:00:00,669 --> 00:00:02,209
Ha. What do you mean, why?

2
00:00:02,379 --> 00:00:05,669
There were studies that suggest
many who go into the performing arts...

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:08,630
(Beverley:)...suffer from an external locus
of identity.

4
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:15,266
(Penny:)Yeah, I don't know what that means.

5
00:00:15,809 --> 00:00:19,019
(Beverley:)Well, it means you value yourself
only as others value you...

6
00:00:19,187 --> 00:00:23,067
(Beverley:)...which is often the result
of unmet childhood emotional needs.

7
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:26,653
(Penny:)Oh, well, I had a wonderful childhood.

8
00:00:27,195 --> 00:00:28,695
(Beverley:)Tell me about it.

9
00:00:30,282 --> 00:00:33,412
(Penny:)I know my dad wanted a boy.

10
00:00:33,743 --> 00:00:35,743
[SOBBING]

11
00:00:35,996 --> 00:00:41,046
I... I just... I tried being good at sports,
but I hated getting dirty.

12
00:00:42,210 --> 00:00:44,380
(Beverley:)And then, I'm assuming,
you entered adolescence.

13
00:00:44,546 --> 00:00:48,216
(Penny:)Uh-huh. He called me slugger
until I got my first training bra...

14
00:00:48,383 --> 00:00:52,173
(Penny:)...and then he just stopped
playing catch with me.

15
00:00:52,387 --> 00:00:55,677
(Penny:)I wasn't slugger anymore.

16
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:04,020
(Penny:)Your mother's here.

